    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50225" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰθύ-φαλλος</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fascinum erectum, the phallos
				carried in the festivals of Bacchus</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Cratin.
				14
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>ode and dance</i> performed at such festivals, <i><span class="en">
				Hyp.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				50
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Duris
				13J.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>one who danced in such dance</i>, Hippoloch. ap.<i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				4.129d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Semus
				20
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Democh.
				2
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
			</span></i>: metaph., <i>lewd fellow</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				54.14
			</span></i>.</div>
